
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Parameter retirement / MPU6050 exception (run from the firmware directory):

g++ -std=c++11 -Itest/imu_host -Ilib/ParameterCatalog -Ilib/ParameterStore test/imu_host/parameter_retirement.cpp lib/ParameterCatalog/ParameterCatalog.cpp lib/ParameterStore/ParameterStore.cpp -o /tmp/opendrift-parameters
/tmp/opendrift-parameters

Repeat with -DOPENDRIFT_IMU_MPU6050 to verify that target retains the old controls
and defaults. Tests cover defaults, stale writes, legacy storage import, profile
application, and persistence without touching real NVS or requiring hardware.

Servo output regression (normal targets, no electrical timing simulation):

g++ -std=c++11 -Itest/servo_host -Itest/imu_host -Ilib/Servo test/servo_host/test.cpp lib/Servo/Servo.cpp -o /tmp/opendrift-servo-test
/tmp/opendrift-servo-test

Wi-Fi manager lifecycle (fake radio/netif APIs, not actual DHCP/RF validation):

g++ -std=c++11 -Itest/wifi_host -Itest/imu_host -Ilib/WIFIManager test/wifi_host/test.cpp lib/WIFIManager/WIFIManager.cpp -o /tmp/opendrift-wifi-test
/tmp/opendrift-wifi-test

CH4 interlocks and touch polling suspension:

g++ -std=c++11 -Ilib/DriveArming test/imu_host/drive_arming.cpp -o /tmp/opendrift-drive-arming
/tmp/opendrift-drive-arming
g++ -std=c++11 -DOPENDRIFT_BOARD_AMOLED_164 -Itest/imu_host -Ilib/Touch test/imu_host/touch_suspend.cpp lib/Touch/Touch.cpp -o /tmp/opendrift-touch-suspend
/tmp/opendrift-touch-suspend
